  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Lead: The player to the dealer's left plays any card from their hand. For example, a 5.\n2. Matching: The next player must play a 5 if they have one. Each subsequent player must match that rank.\n3. The Rhyme: With each card played, the player MUST say the corresponding line:\n   - 1st Card: 'There's as good as 5 can be.'\n   - 2nd Card: 'There's a 5 as good as he.'\n   - 3rd Card: 'There's the best of all the three.'\n   - 4th Card: 'And there's the Earl of Coventry!'\n4. Re-Lead: The person who plays the 4th card of the rank (the Earl) immediately leads any card they wish to start the next sequence.",
    Player: "1. Lead: The player to the dealer's left plays any card from their hand. For example, a 5.\n2. Matching: The next player must play a 5 if they have one. Each subsequent player must match that rank.\n3. The Rhyme: With each card played, the player MUST say the corresponding line:\n   - 1st Card: 'There's as good as 5 can be.'\n   - 2nd Card: 'There's a 5 as good as he.'\n   - 3rd Card: 'There's the best of all the three.'\n   - 4th Card: 'And there's the Earl of Coventry!'\n4. Re-Lead: The person who plays the 4th card of the rank (the Earl) immediately leads any card they wish to start the next sequence.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand.',
    gameplay: "1. Lead: The player to the dealer's left plays any card from their hand. For example, a 5.\n2. Matching: The next player must play a 5 if they have one. Each subsequent player must match that rank.\n3. The Rhyme: With each card played, the player MUST say the corresponding line:\n   - 1st Card: 'There's as good as 5 can be.'\n   - 2nd Card: 'There's a 5 as good as he.'\n   - 3rd Card: 'There's the best of all the three.'\n   - 4th Card: 'And there's the Earl of Coventry!'\n4. Re-Lead: The person who plays the 4th card of the rank (the Earl) immediately leads any card they wish to start the next sequence.",
    keyRules: [
      'If you do not have a card of the rank currently being played, you pass your turn.',
      'If NO ONE can play the next card in the sequence (e.g., the remaining 3s have already been played earlier), the last person to play a card of that rank leads a new card.',
      'Verbal accuracy is traditionally required; failure to say the rhyme correctly may result in a small penalty in home rules.',
